Describe a time when you made a decision to wait for something

I’d like to talk about a time when I applied for an internship at an international technology company.

This happened when I was in my final year at university. At that time, I was required to complete an internship related to my major, which is software engineering. Since I had always wanted to work in a professional and international environment, I decided to apply for several internship programs at large tech companies.

To be honest, preparing for the application process was quite stressful. I spent several months improving my resume, practicing technical interview questions, and waiting for suitable internship openings. As soon as I saw the recruitment announcement from one company I was really interested in, I immediately submitted my application.

The recruitment process was quite competitive and lasted for around one or two months. I had to go through multiple rounds, including interviews and technical assessments. At some points, I felt really nervous because there were many talented candidates applying for the same position, so I knew my chances were quite slim.

After finishing the final interview, I had to wait about two weeks for the result. Honestly, that was probably the most stressful part because I kept checking my email every day. Fortunately, my patience paid off. One day, I received an email congratulating me on being selected for the internship position, and I was absolutely thrilled at that moment.

This experience taught me that patience and persistence are extremely important. Even when things seem difficult or competitive, staying determined and continuing to work hard can eventually lead to good results. I believe this lesson will continue to help me in both my studies and my future career.
